+> "currently both our validate plan and confirm has some typescript logic, that if true, it returns their error early, this is good because it prevents the llm agent to run if there are typescript stuff wrong. This is not what i want. What i want instead is that all typescript return early paths, accumluate and reurn together, so that they do what they were supposed todo, which is preventing not needed llm calls, but other typescript calls do not need to be prevented. Therfore the logic for validate plan is: First all typescript earlier catchers, and only if no catched then continue with the llm part. And for confirm it shall be first the calling of the check mcp like allready done, if that fails, then return early, then after that run all the typescript earlier catchers, and only if they didnt catch run the llm."
